ackets with the Qualitative service type (ServiceTypeQualitative). The Packet Scheduler inserts the corresponding priority value in the Layer-2 header of the packets.\r\n\r\nIf you enable this setting, you can change the default priority value associated with the Qualitative service type.\r\n\r\nIf you disable this setting, the system uses the default priority value of 0.\r\n\r\nImportant: If the Layer-2 priority value for this service type is specified in the registry for a particular network adapter, this setting is ignored when configuring that network adapter.\r\n ","categoryId":"67c06154-a798-44bb-83c8-d706a3709c10","baseUri":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/ADMX_QOS/QosServiceTypeQualitative_PV","rootDefinitionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv","uxBehavior":"toggle","infoUrls":["https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-admx-qos#admx-qos-qosservicetypequalitative-pv"],"applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv_0","options":[{"itemId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv_0","displayName":"Disabled","dependedOnBy":[]},{"itemId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv_1","displayName":"Enabled","dependedOnBy":[{"dependedOnBy":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv_qospriorityvalue","required":true}]}]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSimpleSettingDefinition","id":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv_qospriorityvalue","name":"QosPriorityValue","displayName":"Priority value (Device)","categoryId":"67c06154-a798-44bb-83c8-d706a3709c10","baseUri":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/ADMX_QOS/QosServiceTypeQualitative_PV","rootDefinitionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypequalitative_pv","uxBehavior":"default","applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"dependedOnBy":[]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSimpleSettingDefinition","id":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypecontrolledload_pv_qospriorityvalue","name":"QosPriorityValue","displayName":"Priority value (Device)","categoryId":"67c06154-a798-44bb-83c8-d706a3709c10","baseUri":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/ADMX_QOS/QosServiceTypeControlledLoad_PV","rootDefinitionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypecontrolledload_pv","uxBehavior":"default","applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"dependedOnBy":[]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationChoiceSettingDefinition","id":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypeguaranteed_pv","name":"QosServiceTypeGuaranteed_PV","displayName":"Guaranteed service type","description":"Specifies an alternate link layer (Layer-2) priority value for packets with the Guaranteed service type (ServiceTypeGuaranteed). The Packet Scheduler inserts the corresponding priority value in the Layer-2 header of the packets.\r\n\r\nIf you enable this setting, you can change the default priority value associated with the Guaranteed service type.\r\n\r\nIf you disable this setting, the system uses the default priority value of 0.\r\n\r\nImportant: If the Layer-2 priority value for this service type is specified in the registry for a particular network adapter, this setting is ignored when configuring that network adapter.\r\n ","categoryId":"67c06154-a798-44bb-83c8-d706a3709c10","baseUri":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/ADMX_QOS/QosServiceTypeGuaranteed_PV","rootDefinitionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypeguaranteed_pv","uxBehavior":"toggle","infoUrls":["https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-admx-qos#admx-qos-qosservicetypeguaranteed-pv"],"applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypeguaranteed_pv_0","options":[{"itemId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypeguaranteed_pv_0","displayName":"Disabled","dependedOnBy":[]},{"itemId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypeguaranteed_pv_1","displayName":"Enabled","dependedOnBy":[{"dependedOnBy":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypeguaranteed_pv_qospriorityvalue","required":true}]}]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationChoiceSettingDefinition","id":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypenonconforming","name":"QosServiceTypeNonConforming","displayName":"Non-conforming packets","description":"Specifies an alternate link layer (Layer-2) priority value for packets that do not conform to the flow specification. The Packet Scheduler inserts the corresponding priority value in the Layer-2 header of the packets.\r\n\r\nIf you enable this setting, you can change the default priority value associated with nonconforming packets.\r\n\r\nIf you disable this setting, the system uses the default priority value of 0.\r\n\r\nImportant: If the Layer-2 priority value for nonconforming packets is specified in the registry for a particular network adapter, this setting is ignored when configuring that network adapter.\r\n ","categoryId":"67c06154-a798-44bb-83c8-d706a3709c10","baseUri":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/ADMX_QOS/QosServiceTypeNonConforming","rootDefinitionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypenonconforming","uxBehavior":"toggle","infoUrls":["https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-admx-qos#admx-qos-qosservicetypenonconforming"],"applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_qos_qosservicetypenonconforming_0","options":[{"itemId":"